§ `Sections 831 to 838 -- Application of other sections, release, powers of the appeal court, enforcement`

-- 831 The provisions of sections 816, 817, 819 and 825 apply, with such modifications as the circumstances require, in respect of an appeal under section 830, except that on receiving an application by the person having the custody of an appellant described in section 819 to appoint a date for the hearing of the appeal, the appeal court shall, after giving the prosecutor a reasonable opportunity to be heard, give such directions as it thinks necessary for expediting the hearing of the appeal.
-- src:17266 | 831 The provisions of sections 816, 817, 819 and 825 apply, with such modifications as the circumstances require, in respect of an appeal under section 830, except that on receiving an application by the person having the custody of an appellant described in section 819 to appoint a date for the hearing of the appeal, the appeal court shall, after giving the prosecutor a reasonable opportunity to be heard, give such directions as it thinks necessary for expediting the hearing of the appeal.
@ref Criminal Code s 831 (src:17266)
GIVEN `the appeal is an appeal under section 830` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the section number` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 831 the provision applies to the appeal` MEANS
    IF `the appeal is an appeal under section 830` AND (`the section number` EQUALS 816 OR `the section number` EQUALS 817 OR `the section number` EQUALS 819 OR `the section number` EQUALS 825)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The provisions of sections 816, 817, 819 and 825 apply ... in respect of an appeal under section 830"

@ref Criminal Code s 831 (src:17266)
-- Fork F-831: "except that" is read as replacing the duty of section 819(2) to fix a date by a duty to give directions only; the other reading adds the directions to the date-fixing duty.
GIVEN `the appeal court has received an application by the person having the custody of an appellant described in section 819 to appoint a date for the hearing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appeal court has given the prosecutor a reasonable opportunity to be heard` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 831 the appeal court is required to give such directions as it thinks necessary for expediting the hearing of the appeal` MEANS
    IF `the appeal court has received an application by the person having the custody of an appellant described in section 819 to appoint a date for the hearing` AND `the appeal court has given the prosecutor a reasonable opportunity to be heard`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "on receiving an application ... the appeal court shall, after giving the prosecutor a reasonable opportunity to be heard"

-- 832(1) If a notice of appeal is filed under section 830, the appeal court may, if the defendant is the appellant, make a release order as provided in section 816 or, in any other case, order that the appellant appear before a justice and enter into a recognizance as provided in section 817.
