         WHEN `s 834(1) make any other order in relation to the matter or with respect to costs` THEN IF `the appeal court considers the order proper` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any other order ... that it considers proper"
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "When a notice of appeal is filed pursuant to section 830"

