§ `Section 839 -- Appeals to the Court of Appeal`

-- 839(1) Subject to subsection (1.1), an appeal to the court of appeal as defined in section 673 may, with leave of that court or a judge thereof, be taken on any ground that involves a question of law alone, against (a) a decision of a court in respect of an appeal under section 822; or (b) a decision of an appeal court under section 834, except where that court is the court of appeal.
-- src:17292 | Appeal on question of law
-- src:17293 | 839 (1) Subject to subsection (1.1), an appeal to the court of appeal as defined in section 673 may, with leave of that court or a judge thereof, be taken on any ground that involves a question of law alone, against
-- src:17294 | (a) a decision of a court in respect of an appeal under section 822; or
-- src:17295 | (b) a decision of an appeal court under section 834, except where that court is the court of appeal.
@ref Criminal Code s 839(1) to s 839(1)(b) (src:17292-17295)
DECLARE `s 839(1) decision` IS ONE OF
    `s 839(1)(a) a decision of a court in respect of an appeal under section 822`
    `s 839(1)(b) a decision of an appeal court under section 834`
    `s 839(1) another decision`

@ref Criminal Code s 839(1) (src:17292-17293)
-- @name-test: flipped to NOTHING; gates "on any ground that involves a question of law alone" and "with leave of that court or a judge thereof" (fork F-839-1); the "except where that court is the court of appeal" limb is closed by the text and sits in the helper s 839(1) the named decision may be appealed
GIVEN decision IS A `s 839(1) decision`
      `the ground involves a question of law alone` IS A BOOLEAN
      `leave is given by the court of appeal or a judge of it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appeal court is the court of appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 839(1) an appeal to the court of appeal may be taken against the decision` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the ground involves a question of law alone` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "on any ground that involves a question of law alone"
        IF NOT `leave is given by the court of appeal or a judge of it` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "with leave of that court or a judge thereof"
        IF `s 839(1) the decision is one named` decision THEN `s 839(1) the named decision may be appealed` decision `the appeal court is the court of appeal`
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "against (a) ... or (b) ..."

@ref Criminal Code s 839(1) (src:17292-17293)
GIVEN decision IS A `s 839(1) decision`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 839(1) the decision is one named` MEANS
    CONSIDER decision
    WHEN `s 839(1)(a) a decision of a court in respect of an appeal under section 822` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 839(1)(b) a decision of an appeal court under section 834` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 839(1) another decision` THEN FALSE

@ref Criminal Code s 839(1) (src:17292-17293)
-- @name-test: kept JUST FALSE, gate closed by the text: "except where that court is the court of appeal"
GIVEN decision IS A `s 839(1) decision`
      `the appeal court is the court of appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 839(1) the named decision may be appealed` MEANS
    CONSIDER decision
    WHEN `s 839(1)(a) a decision of a court in respect of an appeal under section 822` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 839(1)(b) a decision of an appeal court under section 834` THEN IF `the appeal court is the court of appeal` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE JUST TRUE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except where that court is the court of appeal"
    WHEN `s 839(1) another decision` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "against (a) ... or (b) ..."

-- 839(1.1) An appeal to the Court of Appeal of Nunavut may, with leave of that court or a judge of that court, be taken on any ground that involves a question of law alone, against a decision of a judge of the Court of Appeal of Nunavut acting as an appeal court under subsection 812(2) or 829(2).
-- src:17296 | Nunavut
-- src:17297 | (1.1) An appeal to the Court of Appeal of Nunavut may, with leave of that court or a judge of that court, be taken on any ground that involves a question of law alone, against a decision of a judge of the Court of Appeal of Nunavut acting as an appeal court under subsection 812(2) or 829(2).
@ref Criminal Code s 839(1.1) (src:17296-17297)
-- @name-test: flipped to NOTHING; gates "with leave of that court or a judge of that court" and "on any ground that involves a question of law alone" (fork F-839-1.1)
GIVEN `the ground involves a question of law alone` IS A BOOLEAN
      `leave is given by the Court of Appeal of Nunavut or a judge of it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision is a decision of a judge of the Court of Appeal of Nunavut acting as an appeal court under subsection 812(2) or 829(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 839(1.1) an appeal to the Court of Appeal of Nunavut may be taken against the decision` MEANS
    IF `the ground involves a question of law alone` AND `leave is given by the Court of Appeal of Nunavut or a judge of it` AND `the decision is a decision of a judge of the Court of Appeal of Nunavut acting as an appeal court under subsection 812(2) or 829(2)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "with leave ... on any ground that involves a question of law alone, against a decision of a judge of the Court of Appeal of Nunavut acting as an appeal court under subsection 812(2) or 829(2)"

-- 839(2) Sections 673 to 689 apply with such modifications as the circumstances require to an appeal under this section.
-- src:17298 | Sections applicable
-- src:17299 | (2) Sections 673 to 689 apply with such modifications as the circumstances require to an appeal under this section.
@ref Criminal Code s 839(2) (src:17298-17299)
GIVEN `the appeal is an appeal under section 839` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the section number` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 839(2) the provision applies to the appeal` MEANS
    IF `the appeal is an appeal under section 839` AND `the section number` AT LEAST 673 AND `the section number` AT MOST 689
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Sections 673 to 689 apply ... to an appeal under this section"

-- 839(3) Notwithstanding subsection (2), the court of appeal may make any order with respect to costs that it considers proper in relation to an appeal under this section.
-- src:17300 | Costs
-- src:17301 | (3) Notwithstanding subsection (2), the court of appeal may make any order with respect to costs that it considers proper in relation to an appeal under this section.
@ref Criminal Code s 839(3) (src:17300-17301)
-- @name-test: no JUST FALSE branch; named for a power, answers NOTHING where the order is not one the court considers proper
GIVEN `the appeal is an appeal under section 839` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court of appeal considers the order proper` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 839(3) the court of appeal may make the order with respect to costs` MEANS
    IF `the appeal is an appeal under section 839` AND `the court of appeal considers the order proper`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any order with respect to costs that it considers proper in relation to an appeal under this section"

-- 839(4) The decision of the court of appeal may be enforced in the same manner as if it had been made by the summary conviction court before which the proceedings were originally heard and determined.
-- src:17302 | Enforcement of decision
-- src:17303 | (4) The decision of the court of appeal may be enforced in the same manner as if it had been made by the summary conviction court before which the proceedings were originally heard and determined.
@ref Criminal Code s 839(4) (src:17302-17303)
-- @name-test: no JUST FALSE branch; named for a power, answers NOTHING outside a decision of the court of appeal
GIVEN `it is a decision of the court of appeal under section 839` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 839(4) the decision may be enforced in the same manner as if it had been made by the summary conviction court` MEANS
    IF `it is a decision of the court of appeal under section 839`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The decision of the court of appeal"

-- 839(5) The Attorney General of Canada has the same rights of appeal in proceedings instituted at the instance of the Government of Canada and conducted by or on behalf of that Government as the Attorney General of a province has under this Part.
-- src:17304 | Right of Attorney General of Canada to appeal
-- src:17305 | (5) The Attorney General of Canada has the same rights of appeal in proceedings instituted at the instance of the Government of Canada and conducted by or on behalf of that Government as the Attorney General of a province has under this Part.
@ref Criminal Code s 839(5) (src:17304-17305)
GIVEN `the proceedings were instituted at the instance of the Government of Canada and conducted by or on behalf of that Government` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 839(5) the Attorney General of Canada has the same rights of appeal as the Attorney General of a province` MEANS
    IF `the proceedings were instituted at the instance of the Government of Canada and conducted by or on behalf of that Government`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in proceedings instituted at the instance of the Government of Canada and conducted by or on behalf of that Government"

§ `Section 840 -- Fees and allowances`

-- 840(1) Subject to subsection (2), the fees and allowances mentioned in the schedule to this Part are the fees and allowances that may be taken or allowed in proceedings before summary conviction courts and justices under this Part.
-- src:17308 | Fees and allowances
-- src:17309 | 840 (1) Subject to subsection (2), the fees and allowances mentioned in the schedule to this Part are the fees and allowances that may be taken or allowed in proceedings before summary conviction courts and justices under this Part.
@ref Criminal Code s 840(1) (src:17308-17309)
-- @name-test: kept JUST FALSE, gate closed by the text: "Subject to subsection (2)" (an order of the lieutenant governor in council under subsection (2) takes the fees and allowances out)
GIVEN `the fee or allowance is mentioned in the schedule to this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the lieutenant governor in council of the province has ordered that it shall not be taken or allowed in the province` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 840(1) the fee or allowance may be taken or allowed in proceedings before summary conviction courts and justices` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the lieutenant governor in council of the province has ordered that it shall not be taken or allowed in the province` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subject to subsection (2) ... shall not be taken or allowed"
        IF `the fee or allowance is mentioned in the schedule to this Part` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the subsection names the fees and allowances in the schedule and does not say that no other may be taken

-- 840(2) The lieutenant governor in council of a province may order that all or any of the fees and allowances mentioned in the schedule to this Part shall not be taken or allowed in proceedings before summary conviction courts and justices under this Part in that province and, when the lieutenant governor in council so orders, he or she may fix any other fees and allowances for any items similar to those mentioned in the schedule, or any other items, to be taken or allowed instead.
-- src:17310 | Order of lieutenant governor in council
-- src:17311 | (2) The lieutenant governor in council of a province may order that all or any of the fees and allowances mentioned in the schedule to this Part shall not be taken or allowed in proceedings before summary conviction courts and justices under this Part in that province and, when the lieutenant governor in council so orders, he or she may fix any other fees and allowances for any items similar to those mentioned in the schedule, or any other items, to be taken or allowed instead.
@ref Criminal Code s 840(2) (src:17310-17311)
-- @name-test: no JUST FALSE branch; named for a power, answers NOTHING outside the lieutenant governor in council of a province
GIVEN `it is the lieutenant governor in council of a province` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 840(2) the lieutenant governor in council may order that all or any of the fees and allowances shall not be taken or allowed in the province` MEANS
    IF `it is the lieutenant governor in council of a province`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The lieutenant governor in council of a province"

@ref Criminal Code s 840(2) (src:17310-17311)
-- @name-test: listed, where/when/upon kind (F-840-2): "when the lieutenant governor in council so orders" answers JUST FALSE
GIVEN `it is the lieutenant governor in council of a province` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the lieutenant governor in council has ordered that all or any of the fees and allowances shall not be taken or allowed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 840(2) the lieutenant governor in council may fix other fees and allowances to be taken or allowed instead` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `it is the lieutenant governor in council of a province` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The lieutenant governor in council of a province"
        IF NOT `the lieutenant governor in council has ordered that all or any of the fees and allowances shall not be taken or allowed` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "when the lieutenant governor in council so orders"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
